<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ADDED 17 Oct 2026 - DoxyPEP widget rebuilt around a countdown ring.

     WHY THE ROOT IS A FrameLayout. The ring needs its sweep and its centre text
     to sit on top of each other, which wants nesting - and nesting is the one
     thing this app's widget layouts cannot do. L-076: nested containers do not
     inflate in a widget RemoteViews layout here (clinic_card_widget shipped one
     and rendered "Can't load widget"; a ViewFlipper reintroduced it and broke
     again), enforced by widgetTapAndFallbackGuard.test.js. So this is the ONE
     ViewGroup, and every child is positioned into it with layout_gravity rather
     than nested inside a second container.

     WHY THAT IS ALSO BETTER THAN A LinearLayout COLUMN. FrameLayout places top,
     centre and bottom independently, so the three bands do not have to sum to
     the widget's height. A vertical stack has to fit exactly, and the audit found
     this layout overflowing its 2-cell box - which clipped content off BOTH ends
     because the root gravity was "center". Here the ring is always centred and
     the text always sits at the bottom, whatever the eyebrow does.

     WHY THE TITLE IS A 12sp EYEBROW. "DoxyPEP Window" at 16sp measured 264px
     into a 212px field and needed ~9.8sp to fit on one line - i.e. it could not
     fit at any legible size. That is pool item t115, and it is why the ring
     replaced it rather than merely joining it: the word "Window" was never
     carrying information. maxLines is 2 because the Redacted tier renders its
     line into this same view.

     WHY THE COUNTDOWN IS BELOW THE RING AND NOT IN IT. The platform's own
     duration format for a 72-hour PEP window is "2d 23:59:59" - about 162px at
     12sp - against a 154px circle interior at this ring size. It cannot be
     fitted without dropping below the 12sp legibility floor, and
     RemoteViews.setChronometer's format argument is a single-string template, so
     the components cannot be selected. So the ring's centre carries the STATUS
     WORD (short, and colour is doing the urgency work anyway) and the live
     countdown gets the full 77dp width underneath it, where any format fits.

     REWRITTEN 20 Oct 2026, and the reason is the same measurement. The status
     word is no longer INSIDE the ring either: "no window" is about 134px at
     12sp, and the hole in the 44dp ring is 88px - so the owner's own wording,
     "no" over "window", would have had to be set at 8sp to fit in the hole.
     Tiny type on a home screen is not a solution, so the status moved BELOW the
     ring, where it has the whole card width and can be 12sp on two centred
     lines. The ring keeps its shape and its sweep; the word sits under it.

     The ring is at the TOP of the card rather than centred, because the bands
     below it (status, countdown, evidence) are what the card is read for, and a
     centred ring would push the countdown off the bottom of a 2-cell card. -->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/widget_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:padding="16dp"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_background">

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_doxy_title"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|start"
         android:text="DoxyPEP"
         android:textSize="16sp"
         android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
         android:textStyle="bold"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:breakStrategy="simple" />

    <!-- 50dp, at the top of the card. Same geometry as the Next Dose ring,
         because both now carry a countdown in the middle: the platform's
         format is the whole duration, and the owner's instruction is that the
         countdown belongs in the ring.

         The drawable is innerRadius 21dp + thickness 4dp, so the hole is
         exactly 42dp and the drawable and the view are the same size - a
         shape drawable is drawn at its own size and CLIPPED if it is bigger. -->
    <ProgressBar
        android:id="@+id/widget_doxy_ring"
        style="@style/ShosWidgetRing"
        android:layout_width="50dp"
        android:layout_height="50dp"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="26dp"
        android:rotation="-90"
        android:max="100" />

    <!-- A real Chronometer, not a pushed string. It ticks in the LAUNCHER
         process, so the countdown is live every second with no app process, no
         alarm and no wake lock - which is what lets the ring arc step coarsely
         on a schedule while the number stays honest.

         It sits in the RING's centre (the owner's instruction, 20 Oct), which
         is why the ring is 50dp: the 72-hour window's format is
         "2d 23:59:59", and that needs a 42dp hole to sit in without shrinking
         into illegibility.

         The width is FIXED and equal to the ring's hole, which is what makes
         the autosize work: autoSize measures the view's own width, so a
         wrap_content view would measure its own text and could never shrink
         it. -->
    <Chronometer
        android:id="@+id/widget_doxy_countdown"
        android:layout_width="42dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="43dp"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textStyle="bold"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:autoSizeTextType="uniform"
        android:autoSizeMaxTextSize="12sp"
        android:autoSizeMinTextSize="9sp"
        android:autoSizeStepGranularity="1sp"
        android:clickable="false"
        android:focusable="false" />

    <!-- The status word that goes IN the ring, for the one state with no
         countdown to show: EXPIRED, where the countdown would be a negative
         duration. The same shape as the Next Dose card's ring label, and for
         the same reason - a Chronometer and a TextView are different view
         types, so the provider shows one and hides the other. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_doxy_ring_label"
        android:layout_width="42dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="43dp"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textStyle="bold"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:autoSizeTextType="uniform"
        android:autoSizeMaxTextSize="12sp"
        android:autoSizeMinTextSize="9sp"
        android:autoSizeStepGranularity="1sp" />

    <!-- The status word, centred under the ring - it gets the room the
         countdown used to take. "Active" and "Expired" are short, and the
         provider recolours this per state, so the status is also the
         accessibility text for the colour, never colour alone.

         maxLines is 2, not 1: "NO WINDOW" on one line was cut to "NO WINDO..."
         because it does not fit the ring's hole, and the owner asked for it
         centred on two lines ("no" over "window") on 20 Oct. Two short lines
         read as one phrase. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_doxy_status"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="80dp"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:text="no window"
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textStyle="bold"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:breakStrategy="simple" />

    <!-- ADDED 9 Oct 2026 (t093), KEPT: the stored date of the encounter that
         opened the window, so the widget shows WHY a window exists. Unchanged in
         substance - an exposure DATE is identifying, so the provider still hides
         it at the Redacted tier.

         It is anchored to the BOTTOM, so the two-line "no window" status can
         never grow down into it. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_doxy_evidence"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="bottom|center_horizontal"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="11sp"
        android:autoSizeTextType="uniform"
        android:autoSizeMaxTextSize="11sp"
        android:autoSizeMinTextSize="9sp"
        android:autoSizeStepGranularity="1sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_muted"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:breakStrategy="simple" />
</FrameLayout>
